  "body": "The Alibaba field descriptions shipped in 4.38.0 said a Coding Plan key is *\"rejected by the Token Plan endpoints\"*. Alibaba's own documentation describes the real failure mode differently, and worse: pairing a plan with the wrong endpoint **bills pay-as-you-go rather than drawing on the subscription**, under a doc heading literally titled \"Unexpected charges with a Coding Plan\".\n\n**\"Rejected\" is a failure you notice immediately. Silent billing is one you notice on an invoice.** Someone holding a Coding Plan subscription who configures the Token Plan provider — an easy mistake, since both are labelled Alibaba and both take an Alibaba key — gets charged per token for work their subscription already covers.\n\n## What changed\n\nCopy only, no behaviour change:\n\n- Both **Token Plan** descriptions now state they bill per token and point a subscriber at the Coding Plan provider instead.\n- Both **Coding Plan** descriptions warn against using the key anywhere else.\n- `.env.example` carries the same correction, replacing the inaccurate \"rejected by the Token Plan endpoints\" line.\n\nThe four-provider split already makes the correct pairing the default. This makes the incorrect one legible.\n\n## Verification\n\n```\nruff format / ruff check / ty: clean\npytest: 3311 passed, 6 failed\n```\n\nThe 6 are the documented PowerShell installer baseline, identical on unmodified `main` in the same shell.\n\nSource: [alibabacloud.com/help/en/model-studio/coding-plan](https://www.alibabacloud.com/help/en/model-studio/coding-plan) and the `help.aliyun.com` CN mirror of the same page.\n\n## Residual risks\n\nNone. Documentation copy only; no code path changes.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
