    "message": "fix(providers): Alibaba plan/endpoint mismatch bills silently, say so\n\nThe Alibaba field descriptions said a Coding Plan key is \"rejected by the\nToken Plan endpoints\". Alibaba's own documentation describes the real failure\nmode differently, and worse: pairing a plan with the wrong endpoint bills\npay-as-you-go rather than drawing on the subscription, under a doc heading\nliterally titled \"Unexpected charges with a Coding Plan\".\n\n\"Rejected\" is a failure you notice immediately. Silent billing is one you\nnotice on an invoice. Someone holding a Coding Plan subscription who\nconfigures the Token Plan provider — an easy mistake, since both are labelled\nAlibaba and both take an Alibaba key — gets charged per token for work their\nsubscription already covers.\n\nCopy only: both Token Plan descriptions now say what they bill and point a\nsubscriber at the Coding Plan provider instead, the Coding Plan descriptions\nwarn against moving the key elsewhere, and .env.example carries the same\ncorrection. No behavior change; the four-provider split already makes the\nright pairing the default, this makes the wrong one legible.\n\nSource: alibabacloud.com/help/en/model-studio/coding-plan and the\nhelp.aliyun.com CN mirror of the same page.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
